WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.120
Oh, crap!

3
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:20.990
Cobra's dead!

4
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.740
Not just dead,
he was murdered!

5
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.120
I-I mean, I never
liked the guy,

6
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.070
but I didn't want him to get
whacked by eldritch demons!

7
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.360
This is sick! I was
not supposed to see that!

8
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:49.510
[WAPOL] I figured
the World Government

9
00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.220
had something
seedy going on,

10
00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.680
but not whatever
the hell that was!

11
00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.110
Who is that guy?

12
00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.110
I'm screwed! I'm dead!

13
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.460
<b>The Round Table
Conference Room</b>

14
00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:08.330
No King Cobra, and no
King Wapol today, either.

15
00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.370
[ROYAL A] We just received
word that their highnesses

16
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.560
wish for you to begin
the meeting without them.

17
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.060
Seems that big speech
wore King Cobra out,

18
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.100
let him have a nap!

19
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.470
[ROYALS chuckle]

20
00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.790
He must be satisfied

21
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.710
now that the matter
of the Warlords is closed.

22
00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.470
That must be it!

23
00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.370
[chuckles] Well then, let's
look at the rest of the agenda.

24
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.480
The Four-Nation Alliance
in the North Blue

25
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.110
is calling for independence.

26
00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.360
♪ time to mambo! Let's
shake away the sorrow! ♪

27
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.710
The council will be
over soon enough.

28
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.570
Let's wait at the port where
those cretins won't come.

29
00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:41.450
Alright.

30
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.330
[FUKABOSHI] What's wrong?

31
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.520
Before we leave,

32
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.210
I wanted to say a few
words to Princess Vivi.

33
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.810
I wonder where she ran off to.

34
00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:57.600
<b>Guest Room
Pangaea Castle</b>

35
00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.190
If you think you'll get away
with this, you're insane!

36
00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.390
Untie me now!

37
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.140
Who are you working for?

38
00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.080
I'm going to tell the world
what you've done!

39
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.520
Just you wait and see!

40
00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.560
[laughs]

41
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.840
Y'know, you're too honest
for your own good.

42
00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.550
We can't set you free
after hearing that!

43
00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.790
I like your fire, though.

44
00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.330
<b>Jabra
Cipher Pol Aigis 0</b>

45
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.210
[KALIFA] Hate to break
it to you, Princess,

46
00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.250
but no one is coming for you,
no matter how much you whine.

47
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.880
You'll be reported missing,

48
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.470
then live out the rest
of your days as someone's pet.

49
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.750
<b>Kalifa
Cipher Pol Aigis 0</b>

50
00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:30.220
What?

51
00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:34.160
You're really asking about
someone else right now?

52
00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.420
[sighs] It sounds like there
was another incident with her,

53
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:42.080
but long story short,
she's just fine.

54
00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.260
Thank goodness.

55
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.480
Apparently, a couple of guys
beat up the Celestial Dragon

56
00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.320
who was after her.

57
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.740
[BOTH] We fear nothing 'cause
we work for Straw Hat Luffy!

58
00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:52.860
[SAI, LEO cheer]

59
00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.030
[SAI, LEO laugh]

60
00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:55.030
Luffy!

61
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.450
They made sure everyone
knew what they were about.

62
00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.010
Now it seems the whole
plaza's in an uproar.

63
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.020
And then, to make
matters worse,

64
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:08.880
Fujitora started helping
the Revolutionaries free the slaves.

65
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.430
Ryokugyu didn't take too
kindly to that, of course.

66
00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.240
[JABRA] And that's the story.

67
00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:17.210
It's a damn joke calling
this shitshow a "Reverie."

68
00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.320
[VIVI] I have to escape.

69
00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.660
I'm not going
to kept as some pet!

70
00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.080
Think, Vivi.

71
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.370
– [rumbling]
– [PEOPLE yelling]

72
00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.150
[ALL gasp]

73
00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:40.500
[WAPOL] Someone, help me!
I didn't see anything, I swear!

74
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.420
Wapol!

75
00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:41.860
Wapol?

76
00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.190
[WAPOL] Get out of my way!

77
00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.880
[VIVI] Wait!

78
00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.470
[WAPOL] I didn't do nothin',
do you hear me?

79
00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:55.710
Leave me alone!
Just go away!

80
00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.850
Chapa.

81
00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.310
Anyone wanna guess
what that was about?

82
00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.440
Was that King Wapol?

83
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:08.270
Huh? Uh! Wait a second!

84
00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.690
Where the hell is Vivi?!

85
00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.990
What?!

86
00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.230
[KINDERELLA] You there!

87
00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.110
Huh?

88
00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.030
[SOLDIER C] Oh! Yes,
Queen Kinderella?

89
00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.670
[WAPOL crying]

90
00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.740
Have you seen my husband?

91
00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.120
[SOLDIER C] No,
Your Majesty. Not today.

92
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.210
[WAPOL wails]

93
00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.520
– [KINDERELLA] Ah-ha!
– [SOLDIER C] King Wapol!

94
00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.960
Darling, I've been
looking all over for you!

95
00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.640
Where did you run off to?

96
00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.970
[gasps]

97
00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.700
Why is there a woman
in your mouth?!

98
00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.180
How far are you
planning to run like this?

99
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.530
As far as I can!

100
00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.550
To the ends of the world
where no one will follow me!

101
00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.250
Sounds good to me!
Take me, too!

102
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.570
[screams]

103
00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.160
[KINDERELLA] Are
they eloping?!

104
00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:35.350
[NARRATOR] The murder
of King Cobra was kept a secret,

105
00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:38.630
<b>The Five Elders</b>

106
00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:38.440
so most of the monarchs
at the Reverie prepared to leave

107
00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.300
without a hint that
anything was wrong.

108
00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.060
I demand to see King Cobra!

109
00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.310
[SOLDIER B] We were ordered
not to allow anyone in.

110
00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.520
[SOLDIER C] Leave at once!

111
00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:48.800
[CHAKA] I told you,
our king is in poor health!

112
00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.420
Let me see him, now!

113
00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.770
[SOLDIER C] Get back!
I said, get back!

114
00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:55.500
King Cobra!

115
00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:57.820
[IGARAM] Excuse me!

116
00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.740
Has anyone seen Princess Vivi
from the Kingdom of Alabasta?

117
00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:02.370
I've never seen her!

118
00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:05.820
She looks like this!
Have any of you seen her?

119
00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.530
Where did you go,
Princess Vivi?

120
00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.600
Please be safe.

121
00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:19.480
[WORKER B] Let's hurry up!

122
00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:22.090
[WORKER C] Careful! Those
belong to one of the royal families.

123
00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.510
Don't let them get damaged.

124
00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:24.320
[WORKERS] Right!

125
00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.550
[chuckles]

126
00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.390
[WORKER E] King Tea the Fourth
is on board and waiting!

127
00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.320
Hurry and bring
his belongings!

128
00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.200
[WORKERS] Yes, sir!

129
00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.430
Uh...

130
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.180
[WAPOL] [growls] Gotta say, this is
going better than I expected.

131
00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.440
We should be safe
for the time being.

132
00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.040
[SABO]
But what's the next step?

133
00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:59.380
Tell the world what happened.
The whole story!

134
00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.440
I don't deserve
any of this!

135
00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:03.280
All I did was peep
through a hole in the wall

136
00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.730
and now they wanna kill me!

137
00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:07.570
For the last time,
keep your voice down!

138
00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.080
[WAPOL] Wait a sec!

139
00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:12.280
I just realized I got
a ticket outta this mess!

140
00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.000
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL A ringing]

141
00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:16.000
He won't let me down when
I got a scoop like this!

142
00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.050
You have
a Transponder Snail?

143
00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:20.470
[MORGANS] Oh,
what a pleasant surprise!

144
00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.680
Did you have a nice
time at the Reverie?

145
00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.890
[WAPOL] Let's not talk
about that right now!

146
00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:28.570
Sounds like something
juicy happened. Spill it.

147
00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.700
No can do, buddy.
They'll ice me for sure.

148
00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.760
I'll have to tell you in person!

149
00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.880
But if you hide me,

150
00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.090
I'll give you the scoop
of a lifetime, I swear!

151
00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:40.160
[MORGANS] Fair enough.

152
00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.840
For starters, where
are you right now?

153
00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:46.030
Hey! What do I tell him?
Whose ship are we on?

154
00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:47.700
The Eigis Kingdom's.

155
00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.170
[MORGANS] Interesting.

156
00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.170
We'll swoop in and tell them
we're researching a story.

157
00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.390
Then sneak on my ship,
and don't be seen.

158
00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:56.870
[WAPOL] I owe ya one!

159
00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.440
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL A]
Cu-lick.

160
00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.980
[laughs]

161
00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:04.100
This is big news! Sounds
like things got unhinged!

162
00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.780
Royally unhinged if
a king's life is at stake!

163
00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:10.930
Now this is what
I live for! Ha-ha!

164
00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:14.570
Anyway, what did
you see? Tell me.

165
00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.020
[WAPOL] You
don't wanna know!

166
00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:19.190
And I mean you specifically
don't wanna know, okay?

167
00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:22.220
So go back to your own
kingdom and stop bugging me!

168
00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:25.780
I can't. It was CP0
who captured me.

169
00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.420
Even if I make it back home,

170
00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.400
they'll just take me into
custody again, by force.

171
00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.450
So let me use
your Transponder Snail!

172
00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:33.700
But why?

173
00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:36.810
Because my father
needs to know I'm safe.

174
00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:38.140
He worries about me.

175
00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:42.720
Oh, hell no! Absolutely
not! Don't even try!

176
00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.930
Why not? And what
does it matter to you?

177
00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:00.190
[stomach growls]

178
00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:02.670
<b>The Kingdom of Tajine's Ship
(Ship's Hold)</b>

179
00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:03.020
[BONNEY] Ohh...
I'm so hungry.

180
00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:09.590
<b>The Kingdom of Lulusia's Ship
(Bilge)</b>

181
00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.490
[SABO] I just have to hold
out till I get to Lulusia.

182
00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.480
I'm counting on you, Sabo.

183
00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.590
You must live on!

184
00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.260
[NARRATOR] With the Reverie
coming to a close,

185
00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.610
the monarchs departed
for their homes,

186
00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:30.310
unaware of what happened
behind the scenes,

187
00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:33.400
and of who was stowing
away on their ships.

188
00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:37.280
However, even if the truth was
obscured by the Government,

189
00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.900
the news of King Cobra's
murder spread like wildfire,

190
00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:44.940
as did tidings of Princess
Vivi's disappearance.

191
00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:47.170
<b>The Holy Land
Mary Geoise</b>

192
00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:46.670
[WARCURY] I suppose it
was only a matter of time

193
00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:50.010
before Sabo crossed
our paths like this.

194
00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:52.110
His life has been
intertwined with the "D."

195
00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.450
At nearly every turn.

196
00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.980
[SATURN] Egghead should be
our priority right now.

197
00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.850
It's time to put
that matter to rest.

198
00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:01.890
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL B ringing]

199
00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:02.810
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL B]
Cu-lick.

200
00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.630
[WARCURY] Yes, Great Imu?

201
00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.810
<b>Chamber of Flowers
Pangaea Castle</b>

202
00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.340
[IMU] I wish to use
Vegapunk's invention.

203
00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.360
Let us see how well
the Mother Flame performs.

204
00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.440
We're still not certain
if it can deliver or not.

205
00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.630
Now would be as good
a time as any to find out.

206
00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.970
Let's postpone
our plans for Egghead.

207
00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:23.060
They may change based
on the results of this test.

208
00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:27.070
We'll aim for a forested area.
Testing it at sea won't do.

209
00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:30.070
[IMU] The Kingdom
of Lulusia, then.

210
00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:32.490
Quite a number
of people live there.

211
00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:33.810
[IMU] It matters not.

212
00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.730
As you wish, of course.

213
00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:39.080
The world should be just as
its Creators will it, after all.

214
00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:41.740
But may I ask, why Lulusia?

215
00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.630
[IMU] It's close.

216
00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.030
[NUSJURO] Indeed.

217
00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.180
Understood. We'll make
preparations now.

218
00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:01.500
It won't be long.

219
00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.840
It's just as well,

220
00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.580
there have been signs
of revolt in Lulusia.

221
00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.840
This will set an example
for the rest of the world.

222
00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:09.730
If it works,

223
00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:12.800
we'll have a very powerful
weapon at our disposal.

224
00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.840
And our long-fought battle
will come to an end.

225
00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.790
[IMU] I have one
more request.

226
00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:21.800
[WARCURY] What is it?

227
00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.590
[IMU] I desire Vivi.

228
00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.420
[ALL] As you wish.

229
00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:28.390
<b>St. Jaygarcia Saturn
(Godhead of Science and Defense)</b>

230
00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.270
<b>St. Marcus Mars
(Godhead of Environment)</b>

231
00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.150
<b>St. Topman Warcury
(Godhead of Justice)</b>

232
00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.020
<b>St. Ethanbaron V. Nusjuro
(Godhead of Finance)</b>

233
00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:35.900
<b>St. Shephard Ju Peter
(Godhead of Agriculture)</b>

234
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.750
<b>Marine Headquarters
New World</b>

235
00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.960
[MARINE OFFICER A] I
have a report, Fleet Admiral!

236
00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:54.290
There are revolts in the Tajine
Kingdom and the Eigis Kingdom.

237
00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.730
Our course is clear.

238
00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:57.890
Time to crush every
last one of them!

239
00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:03.880
[bell ringing]

240
00:12:57.970 --> 00:12:59.230
[MARINE C] Move the ammo!

241
00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.830
Deploy the seraphim!
Order a full assault!

242
00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.120
Roger! Prepare the seraphim
for departure, now!

243
00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.150
[NARRATOR] Thanks
to the abolition

244
00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.870
of the Seven Warlords System

245
00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.120
and a recent
increase in uprisings,

246
00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.240
the Navy was busier
than ever before.

247
00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:22.160
However, this was also the start
of a different approach

248
00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.880
and an aggressive
new campaign.

249
00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.580
[MARINES yell]

250
00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.910
<b>Kamabakka Queendom
Peachy Island
Grand Line</b>

251
00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.680
[SABO] As soon as
we arrived at Lulusia,

252
00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.470
King Seki and Princess
Comane were captured.

253
00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:35.000
The citizens were lying
in wait with an ambush.

254
00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.140
They'd had enough.

255
00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.960
Get me out of this cage now!

256
00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:45.010
[CIVILIANS cheering]

257
00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:49.610
They found me
and welcomed me as a hero.

258
00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:50.630
I was lucky.

259
00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.610
Well, I wouldn't call it "luck."

260
00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:53.640
After all you've done,

261
00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:56.330
it's no surprise that
you give people hope.

262
00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.450
When I saw the newspaper,

263
00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.750
I realized it was
more than that.

264
00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:02.780
<b>vNQ:PQi:NJVks,iKz"o;;!
zumrvujOVRk!iLyB5!aQs!
rRewifl:BM84OKbL5qOc3! 4NzbI8BoNQ?feZdt1eSS6E
l'ULZX'"h8pq:'PFJsDhWy
tH4ThY:aJrNAqc.?;TNuyD</b>
<b>King Cobra Assassinated</b>

265
00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.120
They were celebrating
because they thought

266
00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.800
I'd assassinated King Cobra.

267
00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:03.700
<b>vNQ:PQi:NJVks,iKz"o;;!
zumrvujOVRk!iLyB5!aQs!
rRewifl:BM84OKbL5qOc3! 4NzbI8BoNQ?feZdt1eSS6E
l'ULZX'"h8pq:'PFJsDhWy
tH4ThY:aJrNAqc.?;TNuyD</b>
<b>King Cobra Assassinated</b>

268
00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.570
What could I say to them when
they were all cheering for me?

269
00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.810
I wanted to tell them
the truth, of course,

270
00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:13.590
and yet I held my tongue.

271
00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.720
Because I felt their hunger
for revolution.

272
00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:19.160
[DRAGON] Hm?

273
00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:21.150
We can thank Betty for that.

274
00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.310
When they met her,

275
00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:25.640
plenty of them wanted to join
the Revolutionary Army.

276
00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:28.410
Those are the ones I
brought here on the ship.

277
00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:33.150
At the time, I wasn't
able to get my hands

278
00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:35.440
on an encrypted
Transponder Snail.

279
00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.650
Which is why I
didn't contact you.

280
00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:39.970
Not till we set sail at least.

281
00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:44.990
<b>Kamabakka
Queendom</b>
<b>Kingdom of Lulusia</b>

282
00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.730
That's when I sent
you a relay message,

283
00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:44.430
which I'm sure seemed odd.

284
00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:49.230
[SABO] Dragon, it's true
that King Cobra is dead...

285
00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.010
...but I didn't kill him.

286
00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.830
<b>Kamabakka
Queendom</b>

287
00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:56.680
Since it wasn't encrypted,

288
00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:00.800
<b>Kingdom of Lulusia</b>

289
00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.880
the Government likely
intercepted the call

290
00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:01.070
and thought I was in Lulusia.

291
00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.950
But in reality, I was already
out at sea with the enlistees.

292
00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.950
And Lulusia was destroyed when
you were on the call with us.

293
00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.350
My, must have been
traumatic for those on board.

294
00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:17.500
Yeah. Everyone on the ship
went into a panic.

295
00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.930
So many of them had just
left their families behind.

296
00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.470
And then right
before their eyes,

297
00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:25.340
everything was
wiped out in a flash.

298
00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.680
I'm sure they
were devastated.

299
00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.470
Can you try to explain
what you saw?

300
00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.540
A massive shadow
covered the sky.

301
00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:42.060
It came out of nowhere.
And then, only a moment later...

302
00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.640
[DRAGON] What do
you mean, a shadow?

303
00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.100
I couldn't make it out,

304
00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.300
because it was flying
above the clouds.

305
00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.980
But it was something dark,
something unnatural.

306
00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:09.070
The person you saw.

307
00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:11.660
You said their name was
"Imu," is that correct?

308
00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:12.750
Yeah.

309
00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.190
[IVANKOV] Well, this might
sound rather bizarre,

310
00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:17.820
but that name has history.

311
00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.360
Eight hundred years ago,

312
00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.860
there was a ruler among
the First Twenty,

313
00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:25.050
Saint Imu of
the Nerona Dynasty.

314
00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:26.670
[gasps]

315
00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:27.750
[IVANKOV] Look at this.

316
00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:30.420
You've heard the story.

317
00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.880
There is an ability that can make
someone immortal, they say.

318
00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:36.870
And it seems we've
found that someone.

319
00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:38.320
They don't know death,

320
00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:41.990
and they're the one calling
the shots at the top of the world.

321
00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:42.360
[SABO gasps]

322
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.840
You think that's the person
I saw? The same Imu?

323
00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.680
It could be a coincidence,
but that seems unlikely.

324
00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:52.970
The Five Elders, who stand above
even the Celestial Dragons,

325
00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:55.140
humble themselves
before Imu.

326
00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.250
Who else could claim
an authority like that,

327
00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.280
commanding the self-proclaimed
descendants of gods?

328
00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:01.880
[gasps]

329
00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.200
[IVANKOV] One more thing!

330
00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:05.390
And this one is terrifying, too!

331
00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:06.820
That shadow you
saw in the sky

332
00:17:06.820 --> 00:17:09.360
is likely a secret
Government weapon.

333
00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:11.700
But who could create
something so powerful?

334
00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:15.800
A genius, that's who!
What if it was Vegapunk?

335
00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.260
That doesn't make sense.

336
00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.440
Perhaps he could,

337
00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:22.110
but Vegapunk would never design
a weapon to commit mass-murder.

338
00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:23.290
I know!

339
00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:28.430
But in that case, it must
be an Ancient Weapon.

340
00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:33.260
If Imu is an ancient human,
then that's hardly a big leap!

341
00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:37.660
Well, we do know that
the Ancient Weapons exist.

342
00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.280
Robin confirmed as much.

343
00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:43.630
And yet, if the Government's
had one for so long,

344
00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:46.900
then why haven't they
tried to use it before?

345
00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:49.370
And why are they
using it now?

346
00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.280
[NARRATOR] We return
to the present day.

347
00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:02.560
A Celestial Dragon has been
executed in Mary Geoise.

348
00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:04.280
However, this shocking event

349
00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:06.780
will never be reported
to the world.

350
00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.030
[CELESTIAL DRAGON A]
Good riddance!

351
00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:10.450
That traitor sided
against his own people!

352
00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:13.200
Now those filthy creatures
are pushing their luck!

353
00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.690
He got what he deserved!

354
00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.760
[CELESTIAL DRAGON B] Now
we can't even eat properly,

355
00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.710
and it's all his fault!

356
00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:21.990
[NARRATOR] The judge was
a man famous for his exploits

357
00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.890
on an island known
as God Valley.

358
00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:28.800
He is the Supreme Commander
of the Holy Knights.

359
00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:34.790
His name:
Saint Figarland Garling.

360
00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:39.330
And the man he executed was
the defender of the fishmen:

361
00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.950
Saint Donquixote Mjosgard.

362
00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:47.400
Stand up for subhuman scum
and you sink even lower.
